From 783719f0137f6808555099a97ff61bf36d6ca747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:08:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 052/104] demux: ogg: clear the finished flag when a seek
 resets the streams

Demux() counts the active logical streams at the top, before it reads
anything, and treats a count of zero with streams still present as the end
of a chained group: the stream is parked in p_old_stream, the list is torn
down and the pcr offset is moved on. The flag that count reads is only
cleared once a page after the eos page has been paged in, which happens
much later in the same function.

So a seek taken in the gap between the eos page being read and the streams
being torn down - that gap is one pass of the input main loop, but a seek
queued while Demux() is reading the eos page lands squarely in it - reaches
the next Demux() with the flag still set. There is no chained stream there;
the handover just discards the state the seek has finished rebuilding, and
the demuxer restarts from wherever Ogg_FindLogicalStreams can pick a group
up, or gives up and reports the end of the file.

Ogg_ResetStreamsHelper() is on every seek path and already clears the rest
of what the seek invalidates, so clear the flag there too. The skeleton
keeps its flag, exactly as it does where pages after eos clear the others:
there the flag is what says preparsing is done, and clearing it would stop
the demuxer emitting a pcr until an eos page it will never see again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/ogg.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
index 8c0fbed084..b53a69044d 100644
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -727,7 +727,17 @@ static void Ogg_ResetStream( logical_stream_t *p_stream )
 static void Ogg_ResetStreamsHelper( demux_sys_t *p_sys )
 {
     for( int i = 0; i < p_sys->i_streams; i++ )
+    {
+        /* A seek taken once the eos page has been read, but before the streams
+         * have been torn down, must not leave the stream flagged finished:
+         * Demux() counts the active ones before it reads anything, and would
+         * take the chained stream handover for what is only a seek. The
+         * skeleton keeps its flag, as it does when pages follow eos: there it
+         * is what says preparsing is done. */
+        if( p_sys->pp_stream[i] != p_sys->p_skelstream )
+            p_sys->pp_stream[i]->b_finished = false;
         Ogg_ResetStream( p_sys->pp_stream[i] );
+    }
 
     ogg_sync_reset( &p_sys->oy );
     p_sys->i_pcr = VLC_TS_UNKNOWN;
